From: Gerry Hu <gerry@Mac.lan>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:59:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] library: install and update skills from SHA-256 git
 repositories (#5362)

Determine the remote's object format from validated ls-remote object IDs
before initializing the download repository. Match SHA-1 and SHA-256
remotes regardless of the user's default hash, while retaining the SHA-1
init path for older Git and the existing dumb HTTP shallow fallback.
Probe and download share the same timeout budget.

Accept full SHA-256 commit IDs in update checks. Resolve named branches
and tags before treating a hexadecimal ref as pinned, and record the
peeled commit after fetching an annotated tag. Pinned checks now also
query the remote and report an unreachable host as unknown. Update the
Library design reference with these compatibility and failure behaviors.

Regression evidence: before the fix, TestFetchGitObjectFormats and
TestInstallFromGitRepo failed in both directions with mismatched
algorithms; TestGitRemoteHeadSHA256 rejected 64-digit HEAD, branch, tag
and pinned commit IDs. The same scenarios pass after the fix. Tests also
cover off-default refs, unborn HEAD, malformed/mixed object IDs, empty
remotes, probe timeout cleanup, hexadecimal branch/tag movement, dumb
HTTP fallback and a legacy Git wrapper. Tests use local repositories.

Verification used a temporary HOME with GOPATH, GOMODCACHE and GOCACHE
pinned before changing HOME:
- go test ./internal/library -count=1 -timeout=15m: PASS (82.071s).
- go test -race ./internal/library -run
  '^(TestInstallFromGitRepo|TestFetchGit.*|TestGit.*)$' -count=1:
  PASS (19.597s).
- GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.8 go test ./internal/library with the same targeted
  expression after converting comments and test messages to English:
  PASS (13.556s).
- gofmt and git diff --check: PASS.
- go vet ./..., GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./..., and
  GOOS=windows go vet ./...: PASS.
- macOS build, GOOS=linux build -tags nogui and GOOS=windows build: PASS.
- Real Gitea skills/gt probe, install and CheckSkills in an isolated HOME:
  PASS, one candidate, 64-digit commit, current (33.981s total).
  A separate HEAD metadata query took 1.048s.

Full suite on Go 1.26.8 (the project's go.mod version):
GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.8 go test -tags nogui -p 4 -count=1 -timeout=45m ./...:
PASS, all 87 test packages passed, 20 packages had no test files.
No global MAGPIE_ADDR override or test exclusion was used.

Earlier full suite on Go 1.27.3:
go test -tags nogui -p 4 -count=1 -timeout=45m ./...:
85 packages passed, 2 failed, 20 had no test files. Gateway JSON parity
and fuzz-seed failures match #5348; the WSL probe failure matches #3680.
These targeted gateway cases all pass on Go 1.26.8 (1.288s).
GUI TestLaneLimitRoutes matches #5150: its owner fallback reads another
running gateway. The unchanged test passes against a controlled local
404 owner endpoint (0.969s); no global endpoint override was used for
the full suite and no running gateway was changed.

Not run: native Linux/Windows execution, real private SSH authentication.
Cross-platform vet/build results do not establish native runtime behavior.
